      "claim_id": "concurrency-mvcc",
      "text": "InnoDB provides row-level locking and consistent nonlocking multi-version reads, while MyISAM uses table-level locking and its MySQL 8.4 feature table marks MVCC unsupported; InnoDB locking scope can cover scanned records/ranges rather than exactly one row.",
      "source_ids": ["mysql-storage-engines-84", "mysql-myisam-84", "mysql-innodb-consistent-read-84", "mysql-innodb-locks-set-84", "isolated-review"],
